  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed with する as {精読|せいどく}する. Commonly contrasted with {多読|たどく} (extensive reading) and {速読|そくどく} (speed reading). In academic and language learning contexts, {精読|せいどく} emphasizes deep comprehension over quantity.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {精読|せいどく}する (to read carefully/intensively)\n- {原文|げんぶん}を{精読|せいどく}する (to read the original text closely)\n- {精読|せいどく}と{多読|たどく} (intensive and extensive reading)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {多読|たどく}: extensive reading — reading widely for quantity (opposite approach)\n- {熟読|じゅくどく}: reading carefully and thoroughly, very similar to {精読|せいどく} but emphasizes repeated or deep engagement",
